# A voiced line plays only while its bubble is on screen (DSDialogueUGUIHandleAudioPatch). Cengiz's Woodcamp routine
# talks with Bombus at the camp while the player stands about 870 units southwest: the bubbles hang outside the camera
# view, and their clips played anyway (heard by players walking past, "Ich muss weiter" out of nowhere). Talking to
# Cengiz up close must still play every voiced line, his and the hero's.
# Debug build only (the `heard` and `routine` agent commands).
#
# dotnet run --project tools/Drova.TestRunner -c Debug -- tests/scenarios/voice_offscreen.scn

default hero 5
default slot 0
set cengiz 2a21bdef-5ade-4ef6-8a58-a45adb6a7464

launch A
A wait ready=1 timeout=240
A wait saves=separate timeout=1
A load $hero $slot
A wait world=1 timeout=240

A tp 3500 -700
A expect near $cengiz 1000 contains "loaded" timeout=30
A expect ai $cengiz contains "routine=R_Cengiz Normal/AllDay" timeout=30
A heard clear

# `heard` records every clip as voice:played|muted:<clip>.
A expect heard voice:muted:DT_WorldDialogue_Template_WoodcampWorldDialogue_Plh_2_Cengiz contains "Plh_2" timeout=300
A expect heard voice:played == none

A tpnear $cengiz 40 0
sleep 3
A heard clear
A talk $cengiz
A expect heard voice:played contains "WhatsUp" timeout=30
A skip first
A expect dialogue contains "in=0" timeout=120
A expect heard voice:played contains "Run_IchBinNochDabei"
A expect heard voice:muted == none
